G4245.b:
⟪πρέσβυς⟫, -εως, ὁ, poët. form of πρεσβύτης (q.v.),
[in LXX (= πρεσβευτής, an ambassador): ⟦Numbers 21:20|Nu 21:20⟧ (⟦Numbers 21:21|21⟧), al. (⁨מַלְאָךְ⁩), ⟦Isaiah 13:8|Is 13:8⟧ ⟦Isaiah 57:9|57:9⟧ (⁨צִיר⁩), I Mac 9:70, al.;] ⟪an old man⟫. Compar., πρεσβύτερος, -α, -ον, [in LXX chiefly for ⁨זָקֵן⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ of age, ⟪elder⟫: ὁ νἱὸς ὁ π., ⟦Luke 15:25|Lk 15:25⟧; as subst., opp. to νεανίσκοι, ⟦Acts 2:17|Ac 2:17⟧; to νεώτερος, ⟦1 Timothy 5:1|I Ti 5:1⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:2|2⟧; of the religious leaders of the past, ⟦Matthew 15:2|Mt 15:2⟧, ⟦Mark 7:3|Mk 7:3⟧, ⟦Mark 7:5|5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:2|He 11:2⟧ (= οἱ πατέρες, ⟦Hebrews 1:1|He 1:1⟧).
⟪2.⟫ Of dignity, rank or office (as found in π. and Inscr. of civil and religious offices, including priesthood, in Asia Minor and in Egypt; v. Deiss., BS, 154 ff., 233 ff.; LAE, 373);
	⟪(a)⟫ among Jews: ⟦Matthew 16:21|Mt 16:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:47|26:47⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:57|57⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:3|27:3⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:12|12⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:20|20⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:41|41⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:12|28:12⟧, ⟦Mark 8:31|Mk 8:31⟧ ⟦Mark 11:27|11:27⟧ ⟦Mark 14:43|14:43⟧, ⟦Mark 14:53|53⟧ ⟦Mark 15:1|15:1⟧, ⟦Luke 7:3|Lk 7:3⟧ ⟦Luke 9:22|9:22⟧ ⟦Luke 20:1|20:1⟧ ⟦Luke 22:52|22:52⟧, ⟦John 8:9|Jo 8:[9]⟧, ⟦Acts 4:5|Ac 4:5⟧, ⟦Acts 4:8|8⟧, ⟦Acts 4:23|23⟧ ⟦Acts 6:12|6:12⟧ ⟦Acts 23:14|23:14⟧ ⟦Acts 24:1|24:1⟧; τ. Ἰουνδαίων, ⟦Acts 25:15|Ac 25:15⟧; τ. λαοῦ, ⟦Matthew 21:23|Mt 21:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:3|26:3⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:1|27:1⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ among Christians: ⟦Acts 11:30|Ac 11:30⟧ ⟦Acts 14:23|14:23⟧ ⟦Acts 15:2|15:2⟧, ⟦Acts 15:4|4⟧, ⟦Acts 15:6|6⟧, ⟦Acts 15:22|22⟧, ⟦Acts 15:23|23⟧ ⟦Acts 16:4|16:4⟧ ⟦Acts 21:18|21:18⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:17|I Ti 5:17⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:19|19⟧, ⟦Titus 1:5|Tit 1:5⟧, ⟦2 John 1:1|II Jo 1⟧, ⟦3 John 1:1|III Jo 1⟧, ⟦1 Peter 5:1|I Pe 5:1⟧, ⟦1 Peter 5:5|5⟧; τ. ἐκκλησίας, ⟦Acts 20:17|Ac 20:17⟧, ⟦James 5:14|Ja 5:14⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ in the visions of the Apocalypse: ⟦Revelation 4:4|Re 4:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:10|10⟧ ⟦Revelation 5:5|5:5⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:6|6⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:8|8⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:11|11⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:14|14⟧ ⟦Revelation 7:11|7:11⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:13|13⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:16|11:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:3|14:3⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:4|19:4⟧. (On the NT use of this word and its relation to ἐπίσκοπος (q.v.), cf. Lft., Phl., 93 ff., 189 ff.; CGT, Past. Epp., lvi ff.) †

G4250.b:
⟪πρίν⟫,
⟪1.⟫ as adv. of time, ⟪before⟫, ⟪formerly⟫ (cl.; III Mac 5:28 6:4, 31).
⟪2.⟫ As conjc. (cl.), ⟪before⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ after a positive sentence, c. acc. et inf.: ⟦Matthew 26:34|Mt 26:34⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:75|75⟧, ⟦Mark 14:72|Mk 14:72⟧, ⟦Luke 22:61|Lk 22:61⟧, ⟦John 4:49|Jo 4:49⟧ ⟦John 8:58|8:58⟧ (where D. om. γενέσθαι and π. becomes prep. c. gen.; v. Bl., § 69, 7) ⟦John 14:29|14:29⟧, ⟦Acts 2:20|Ac 2:20⟧(LXX), WH, txt.; πρὶν ἤ (not such good Attic in this construction; v. Bl., § 69, 7), ⟦Matthew 1:18|Mt 1:18⟧, ⟦Mark 14:30|Mk 14:30⟧, ⟦Acts 2:20|Ac 2:20⟧, WH, mg., ⟦Acts 7:2|7:2⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ after a negative sentence, πρὶν ἤ: a. subjc. (seq. ἄν, M, Pr., 169), ⟦Luke 2:26|Lk 2:26⟧; c. optat., ⟦Acts 25:16|Ac 25:16⟧.†

G4253.b:
⟪πρό⟫, prep. c. gen.,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨לִפְנֵי⁩;] ⟪before⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of place: ⟦Acts 12:6|Ac 12:6⟧, ⟦Acts 12:14|14⟧ ⟦Acts 14:13|14:13⟧, ⟦James 5:9|Ja 5:9⟧; π. προσώπου (= Heb. ⁨לִפְנֵי⁩, ⟦Deuteronomy 3:18|De 3:18⟧, ⟦Malachi 3:1|Ma 3:1⟧, al.; Bl., § 40, 9), ⟦Matthew 11:10|Mt 11:10⟧, ⟦Mark 1:2|Mk 1:2⟧, ⟦Luke 1:76|Lk 1:76⟧ ⟦Luke 7:27|7:27⟧ ⟦Luke 9:52|9:52⟧ ⟦Luke 10:1|10:1⟧, ⟦Acts 14:13|Ac 14:13⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of time: ⟦Matthew 8:29|Mt 8:29⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:38|24:38⟧, ⟦Luke 11:38|Lk 11:38⟧ ⟦Luke 21:12|21:12⟧, ⟦John 11:55|Jo 11:55⟧ ⟦John 13:1|13:1⟧ ⟦John 17:24|17:24⟧, ⟦Acts 5:36|Ac 5:36⟧ ⟦Acts 21:38|21:38⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:7|I Co 2:7⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 4:5|4:5⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:4|Eph 1:4⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:17|Col 1:17⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:9|II Ti 1:9⟧ ⟦2 Timothy 4:21|4:21⟧, ⟦Titus 1:2|Tit 1:2⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:5|He 11:5⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:20|I Pe 1:20⟧, ⟦Jude 1:25|Ju 25⟧; π. ἐτῶν δεκατεσσάρων, ⟪fourteen years ago⟫, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:2|II Co 12:2⟧; π. προσώπου (v. supr.), ⟦Acts 13:24|Ac 13:24⟧; c. gen. pers., ⟦Matthew 5:12|Mt 5:12⟧, ⟦John 5:7|Jo 5:7⟧ ⟦John 10:8|10:8⟧, ⟦Romans 16:7|Ro 16:7⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:17|Ga 1:17⟧; c. gen. art. inf. (= πρίν; M, Pr., 100; Bl., § 69, 7), ⟦Matthew 6:8|Mt 6:8⟧, ⟦Luke 2:21|Lk 2:21⟧ ⟦Luke 22:15|22:15⟧, ⟦John 1:49|Jo 1:49⟧ ⟦John 13:19|13:19⟧ ⟦John 17:5|17:5⟧, ⟦Acts 23:15|Ac 23:15⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:12|Ga 2:12⟧ ⟦Galatians 3:23|3:23⟧; as in late writers (resembling a Latin idiom but independent of it; B1., § 40, 5; M, Pr., 100 f.; cf. ⟦Amos 1:1|Am 1:1⟧, II Mac 15:36, and for other exx., Soph., Lex., s.v.), πρὸ ἓξ ἡμέρας τοῦ πασχα, ⟪on the sixth day bef. the Passover⟫, ⟦John 12:1|Jo 12:1⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of preference: π. πάντων, ⟦James 5:12|Ja 5:12⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:8|I Pe 4:8⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ in compos.,
	⟪α⟫ c. subst., of position before: προαύλιον, πρόδρομος; priority of rank or order, προπάτωρ; anticipation, πρόγνωσις, πρόνοια;
	⟪β⟫ c. adj., intensity, πρόδηλος;
	⟪γ⟫ c. verb., of place, προάγω, προβαίνω; of preference, προαιρέομαι.†

G4254.b:
⟪προ-άγω⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦1 Samuel 17:16|I Ki 17:16⟧ (⁨נגשׁ⁩), Wi 19:11, al.;]
⟪1.⟫ prop. trans., ⟪to lead on⟫, ⟪lead forth⟫ or ⟪forward⟫: c. acc. pers., ⟦Acts 16:30|Ac 16:30⟧ ⟦Acts 17:5|17:5⟧; of bringing forth to trial, ⟦Acts 12:6|Ac 12:6⟧ (WH, txt., προσάγ-); seq. ἐπί, c. gen. pers., ⟦Acts 25:26|Ac 25:26⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Intrans. (Plat., Polyb., and later writers; v. Bl., § 53, 1; MM, xxi);
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to lead the way⟫, ⟦1 Timothy 1:18|I Ti 1:18⟧ (R, mg.), hence, ⟪to go before⟫, ⟪precede⟫: ⟦Luke 18:39|Lk 18:39⟧; opp. to ἀκολουθέω, ⟦Mark 11:9|Mk 11:9⟧; seq. εἰς, ⟦Matthew 14:22|Mt 14:22⟧, ⟦Mark 6:45|Mk 6:45⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:24|I Ti 5:24⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:18|He 7:18⟧; c. acc. pers., ⟦Matthew 2:9|Mt 2:9⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:9|21:9⟧, ⟦Mark 10:32|Mk 10:32⟧; seq. εἰς, ⟦Matthew 21:31|Mt 21:31⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:32|26:32⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:7|28:7⟧, ⟦Mark 14:28|Mk 14:28⟧ ⟦Mark 16:7|16:7⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to go on⟫, ⟪advance⟫ (Si 20:27): ⟦2 John 1:9|II Jo 9⟧.†

G4291.b:
⟪προ-ΐστημι⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦2 Samuel 13:17|II Ki 13:17⟧, ⟦Proverbs 23:5|Pr 23:5⟧ ⟦Proverbs 26:17|26:17⟧, ⟦Isaiah 43:24|Is 43:24⟧, ⟦Amos 6:10|Am 6:10⟧ (no proper Heb. equiv.), Da LXX Bel 7, I Mac 5:19, IV Mac 11:27*;]
⟪1.⟫ trans. in fut., 1 aor., and mid. 1 aor., ⟪to put before⟫, ⟪set over⟫ (Plat., al.).
⟪2.⟫ Intrans., in pf., plpf., 2 aor. and mid. pres. and impf.;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to preside⟫, ⟪rule⟫, ⟪govern⟫: ⟦Romans 12:8|Ro 12:8⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:17|I Ti 5:17⟧; c. gen., ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:12|I Th 5:12⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:4|I Ti 3:4⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:5|5⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:12|12⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to direct⟫, ⟪maintain⟫: c. gen. rei, καλῶν ἔργων, ⟦Titus 3:8|Tit 3:8⟧, ⟦Titus 3:14|14⟧ (on R, mg., profess honest occupations, v. CGT, in l.; Field, Notes, 223 f.).†
